    'Most sore throats are caused by viruses and clear up on their own with rest and symptom relief, without antibiotics. But if you also have a fever, symptoms do not improve within a few days, or swallowing gets harder, see a doctor to check for a bacterial infection such as strep throat, because untreated it can lead to preventable complications.',
